      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In Part 1 of this series, you will learn how to systematically analyze inference performance and identify where the time is spent.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/amazon/profiling-torchneuron-part-1",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T16:04:43.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T00:37:29.846Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The walkthrough uses AWS Trainium, a purpose-built AI chip for deep learning training and inference workloads, and TorchNeuron , its open source native PyTorch backend.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/amazon/profiling-torchneuron-part-1",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T16:04:43.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T00:37:29.846Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "TorchNeuron supports standard PyTorch workflows on Trainium, including eager execution, torch.compile , and standard PyTorch APIs, with minimal code changes.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/amazon/profiling-torchneuron-part-1",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T16:04:43.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T00:37:29.846Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Additionally, TorchNeuron integrates with Neuron Kernel Interface (NKI) to enable custom operators and performance optimization for Trainium hardware.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/amazon/profiling-torchneuron-part-1",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T16:04:43.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T00:37:29.846Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The Neuron backend uses PyTorch's PrivateUse1 extension point.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/amazon/profiling-torchneuron-part-1",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T16:04:43.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T00:37:29.846Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For details about this extension mechanism, see Facilitating New Backend Integration by PrivateUse1 .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/amazon/profiling-torchneuron-part-1",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T16:04:43.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T00:37:29.846Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "See Step 5: Upload your profile for the UI and command-line instructions.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/amazon/profiling-torchneuron-part-1",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T16:04:43.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-23T00:37:29.846Z"
      },
      {
